  "articleBody": "Thinking about tackling that remodel framing yourself? While it might seem like a good way to save a few bucks, there are some pretty significant hidden dangers that can quickly turn a DIY project into a costly headache. One of the biggest risks is starting demolition without thoroughly checking for electrical wires and plumbing lines. Trust me, hitting a live wire or bursting a pipe is not a fun surprise, and it can cause serious damage and even injury. Another common mistake is cutting too much of the existing wall, especially if it's a load-bearing one. You could compromise the structural integrity of your home, leading to much bigger and more expensive repairs down the road. It’s also easy to misjudge how to properly enlarge or rework an opening without correcting the sill and header layout. These components are vital for supporting the wall above and ensuring everything is stable. Existing walls often hide all sorts of surprises that new-construction framing doesn't, from old wiring to unexpected plumbing routes. Without experience in remodel sequencing and utility coordination, you could easily create more problems than you solve. If your remodel involves load-bearing framing, concealed utilities, or correcting an opening that’s already a bit off, calling in a qualified professional is absolutely the smart move. HH Remodeling LLC has the expertise to handle these complexities safely and efficiently. Give us a call at 303-505-0866 before you start swinging that hammer!",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
